 | Remove user | Admin, owner | Cannot remove the owner; employees lose immediate access to the entity. |
 | Assign role | Admin, owner | Users are **separated by role**; employees receive granular permissions, not admin/owner role. |
 
+## Authentication
+
+Session-based sign-in for staff accounts (Livewire + Bulma, pt-BR first with English fallback).
+
+| Rule | Behaviour |
+| ---- | --------- |
+| Password policy | Minimum 8 characters with letters (mixed case) and numbers; one definition (`Password::defaults()`) shared by registration and reset. |
+| Failed sign-in | Five failed attempts per lowercase e-mail + IP lock that pair for one minute. Failures are written to the audit channel without the e-mail address. |
+| Registration | New accounts are unverified. Registration signs the user in, but the home page requires a verified e-mail. |
+| E-mail verification | Only the signed-in owner of the address can verify it through the signed link; tampered links are rejected. Resending is throttled and does nothing once verified. |
+| Password reset | Answers the same whether or not the e-mail exists; requests are throttled to six per minute. A successful reset rotates the remember token, which signs out "remember me" sessions. |
+| Sign-out | Ends the session and rotates the CSRF token. |
+
